# OpenAPI and SDK

`{{ service_name }}` publishes the unmodified FastAPI OpenAPI 3.1 document directly through
`GET /getOpenApi`.

## Publication

`getOpenApi` and `/getOpenApi` are stable source-defined contracts, not runtime settings. Built-in
`/openapi.json`, `/docs`, and `/redoc` routes are disabled.

The document contains ordinary paths, request schemas, response schemas, summaries, descriptions,
tags, status responses, and standard OAuth2 security metadata. It contains no project extension,
service identity, custom Python metadata, or post-processing mutation.

The canonical `PokerlostOAuth2` security scheme uses the client-credentials flow, `/getToken`, and
the exact local `Scopes` catalog. A protected operation has one non-empty security requirement;
public operations have none. The JSON request schema stays `PokerlostRequest` in both cases.
If the document has no protected operation, the unused scheme may be absent.

## Generation

The authoritative generator reads all available service documents together, skips infrastructure
routes, validates the POST/JSON/envelope contract and global name uniqueness, then writes flat
method/type modules. `PokerlostScopes` is an explicit SDK-owned catalog, not a union inferred from
incomplete production documents. Exact method `__scopes__` metadata comes only from standard
OpenAPI security requirements, and every protected scope must already exist in that SDK catalog.

Manual future-facing method stubs remain outside the generator manifest unless explicitly owned.
They perform ordinary SDK calls when their endpoints exist and never return synthetic success.

## Calls

Inter-service calls use `PokerlostClient` and generated `PokerlostMethod` classes. Every call
serializes `PokerlostRequest`; protected calls pass through retry then authorization middleware,
which adds only the bearer header internally. The complete lifecycle is in
`docs/architecture/inter-service-clients.md`.
